            "tag": 338
          },
          {
            "ind2": " ",
            "ind1": " ",
            "subfield": {
              "code": "a",
              "content": "Cadastral map of the town of Goulburn, Southern New South Wales, 1932."
            },
            "tag": 500
          },
          {
            "ind2": " ",
            "ind1": " ",
            "subfield": {
              "code": "a",
              "content": "Area: covers from Rossiville estate to Goulburn central cemetery and from boundary of parish of Narrangarril  to boundary of Mulwaree Shire."
            },
            "tag": 500
          },
          {
            "ind2": " ",
            "ind1": " ",
            "subfield": {
              "code": "a",
              "content": "Shows named and unnamed streets, numbered and measured allotments, with owners names, reserves for public recreation, rifle range, bird and animal sanctuary, public buildings, churches, hospital, high school, post & telegraph office, court house, cemeteries, girl's hostel, St. Patrick's College, Goulburn West, East and South Public Schools, Southern Railway line and station, Marsden's Bridge, Victoria Park, Manfred Park, Belmore Square, North Gouburn Park, Darling Square, Goulburn Gaol, Presbyterian College, Goulburn War Memorial, and Rocky T.S. Also shows boundaries of parishes Towrang, Warrangarril, Goulburn; Argyle, Camden & King gold field; Mulwaree Shire; Rossiville, Garroorigang and Lansdownde Estates and suburbs Garfield, Eastgrove, Kings Plains and Ifield."
            },
            "tag": 500
          },
          {
            "ind2": " ",
            "ind1": " ",
            "subfield": {
              "code": "a",
              "content": "Contains notes: 'Within', 'Distinctive boundaries', 'Reference notes', Small allotments', 'Road permits' and 'Classified areas'."
